            0.377
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The 4-sided figure obtained (T + U + V) is in fact a square with an area equal to the sum of the areas of the two smaller squares!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.384,
            0.217,
            0.409
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Why?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.415,
            0.846,
            0.455
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As T, U, X and W are all congruent, the sides of this new 4-sided figure all have the same length. Notice the angles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.314,
            0.457,
            0.657,
            0.69
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.314,
                0.457,
                0.657,
                0.69
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_11_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.693,
            0.845,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Explain why all the angles of this new 4-sided figure are right angles and so it is a square."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.742,
            0.845,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Notice that this new square has as its sidelength, the hypotenuse of the right triangle of sides a and b."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.789,
            0.566,
            0.81
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Baudhāyana’s assertion is now clear:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.813,
            0.848,
            0.871
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The area of the square on the hypotenuse = the sum of the areas of T, U, and V = the sum of the areas of V, W, and X = the sum of the areas of the two given squares."
            }
          ]
        },
